WEBVTT

00:01.960 --> 00:03.753
Hey, are you listening?

00:04.629 --> 00:08.383
I told you,
the auto-lock door is not functioning!

00:08.967 --> 00:10.468
Don't make me repeat myself!

00:11.970 --> 00:13.388
I told you last week.

00:14.222 --> 00:17.600
Why do you think
I pay such a high management fee?

00:17.684 --> 00:18.977
What?

00:19.060 --> 00:21.396
Stop messing with me.

00:21.479 --> 00:23.398
Come over and check right now!

00:24.607 --> 00:26.651
Do you hear me?

00:26.735 --> 00:28.361
I'm going to kill you!

02:02.497 --> 02:05.416
June in Morioka, Taichi Kanada.

02:06.417 --> 02:09.546
August in Yokohama, Osamu Shimada.

02:10.588 --> 02:13.550
September in Nagoya, Hiroshi Yamato.

02:14.425 --> 02:17.637
Their cause of death is the same.

02:18.763 --> 02:22.934
They were killed by a Cursed Spirit
at their apartment entrance.

02:23.518 --> 02:26.271
And they complained about the same thing

02:26.354 --> 02:29.107
to the management
weeks before their death.

02:29.774 --> 02:33.153
"The auto-lock door is not functioning."

02:34.529 --> 02:37.949
But the other residents
did not have the same problem.

02:38.032 --> 02:40.743
The dates and locations are different.

02:40.827 --> 02:42.829
Could this be done
by the same Cursed Spirit?

02:43.454 --> 02:44.414
Hey.

02:44.497 --> 02:46.916
Is the Cursed Spirit related
to the auto-lock doors?

02:47.000 --> 02:49.586
Can Cursed Spirits
get caught by the door sensor?

02:49.669 --> 02:51.921
I remember that
they are invisible on camera.

02:52.505 --> 02:54.007
It's not the sensor.

02:54.090 --> 02:58.428
It seems like the door operator system
was affected by the Cursed Spirit.

02:59.012 --> 03:00.263
I see.

03:02.140 --> 03:05.852
We can't determine if the incidents were

03:05.935 --> 03:09.314
done by the same Cursed Spirit
based on the residuals

03:09.397 --> 03:11.608
since the incidents happened a while back.

03:12.108 --> 03:15.612
So I looked for similarities
that connect the three cases.

03:15.695 --> 03:20.074
They all attended
the same junior high for two years.

03:20.158 --> 03:24.037
That means they were cursed back then,

03:24.120 --> 03:26.748
and it took all these years to manifest?

03:26.831 --> 03:27.832
Oh, wow!

03:27.916 --> 03:30.627
Yes, that's possible.

03:31.127 --> 03:33.087
That's why we're going
to their junior high

03:33.171 --> 03:36.841
to speak to the victims'
common acquaintance.

03:37.342 --> 03:41.512
I hope you all can discover
something as Jujutsu Sorcerers.

03:42.180 --> 03:44.432
You're amazing, Kugisaki!

03:45.058 --> 03:46.184
Of course.

03:49.270 --> 03:51.189
SPIRIT LIGHT

03:51.272 --> 03:52.982
MORISHITA'S FUNERAL, 11:00 A.M.

03:53.066 --> 03:54.651
Funeral?

03:55.485 --> 03:57.654
Is that where the acquaintance lives?

03:58.238 --> 04:01.157
It is, but…

04:02.617 --> 04:04.661
What a headache.

04:04.744 --> 04:07.664
He died the same way as the other three.

04:09.540 --> 04:10.875
He's living with his parents

04:10.959 --> 04:12.919
and does not have an auto-lock door,

04:13.002 --> 04:15.588
but he's also killed
at the front entrance.

04:16.798 --> 04:19.050
It seems that when he returned home alone,

04:19.133 --> 04:21.761
he told his family the door wouldn't open

04:21.844 --> 04:24.055
even though it was unlocked.

04:25.932 --> 04:27.308
SAITAMA URAMI EAST JUNIOR HIGH

04:27.392 --> 04:29.477
I talked to his parents,

04:29.560 --> 04:33.064
but they were unsure of his relationship
with the other three victims.

04:34.023 --> 04:35.858
That's our only lead!

04:35.942 --> 04:36.901
Don't mind.

04:36.985 --> 04:39.320
There must be some hints in this school.

04:39.404 --> 04:41.489
I hope so.

04:41.572 --> 04:44.200
Anyway, I have an appointment
with a teacher.

04:44.284 --> 04:46.494
-I'll leave it to you guys.
-Understood.

04:46.577 --> 04:47.620
What?

04:49.539 --> 04:51.791
They are bad students for sure.

04:51.874 --> 04:53.960
-Let's beat them up to reform them.
-Why?

04:54.836 --> 04:56.337
-What?
-What?

04:57.755 --> 04:58.756
What?

05:01.050 --> 05:03.011
Good day to you!

05:04.137 --> 05:06.931
What? They are quite sensible to me.

05:07.015 --> 05:10.852
My strong aura cannot be suppressed.

05:10.935 --> 05:13.271
We haven't seen you
since graduation, Fushiguro!

05:13.354 --> 05:14.522
-What?
-What?

05:18.318 --> 05:21.696
This was my junior high.

05:21.779 --> 05:24.449
This is shocking too,
but that's not the point!

05:24.532 --> 05:28.328
-Look over here!
-What have you done during junior high?

05:28.411 --> 05:30.830
No, it's faster to ask them directly.

05:30.913 --> 05:33.708
Hey, Idiot A and Idiot B,
what did he do to you?

05:33.791 --> 05:35.251
We…

05:35.335 --> 05:39.130
Actually, half of the delinquents
around here

05:39.213 --> 05:41.466
were beaten up by Fushiguro before.

05:41.549 --> 05:42.508
-What?
-What?

05:43.217 --> 05:44.469
-What?
-What?

05:47.597 --> 05:49.474
I beat them up.

05:49.557 --> 05:51.476
Why do you keep stuttering?

05:51.559 --> 05:53.811
-Look here!
-What did you do?

05:53.895 --> 05:55.563
Just what did you do?

05:55.646 --> 05:56.481
Hey!

05:56.564 --> 05:57.482
-What?
-What?

05:57.565 --> 05:58.900
Who are you guys?

05:58.983 --> 06:00.985
Outsiders are not allowed to enter.

06:01.069 --> 06:03.780
Who are you then?

06:03.863 --> 06:06.866
He must be a staff here.
Why are you so fierce?

06:06.949 --> 06:08.743
We have permission to enter the school.

06:08.826 --> 06:12.080
Oh, it's you guys.

06:12.163 --> 06:13.790
You all look so young.

06:14.415 --> 06:17.043
Please wear the visitor pass
around your neck.

06:17.126 --> 06:18.211
Wait.

06:18.753 --> 06:20.254
Are you Fushiguro?

06:21.547 --> 06:22.507
Hello.

06:22.590 --> 06:24.801
-He remembers you.
-He remembers you.

06:24.884 --> 06:27.345
Has he been in this school
for a long time?

06:27.428 --> 06:28.554
I guess so.

06:28.638 --> 06:30.932
Mr. Takeda is a permanent staff.

06:31.015 --> 06:32.850
I'll leave the rest to you, then!

06:32.934 --> 06:34.769
She's neglecting her work duties.

06:35.603 --> 06:38.523
Kanada, Shimada, Yamato,

06:38.606 --> 06:41.025
and now Morishita?

06:41.692 --> 06:44.362
I'm surprised to hear about their passing,

06:44.445 --> 06:48.199
but I can't believe that they have
graduated for almost 20 years.

06:48.866 --> 06:51.994
I still remember them
as if it were just yesterday.

06:52.829 --> 06:56.749
They were not on par with you,
but they were all troublemakers.

06:56.833 --> 06:58.292
What do you want to know?

06:58.960 --> 07:02.922
Were there any strange or bad rumors?
Do they mingle with bad people?

07:03.005 --> 07:05.508
-A troublemaker.
-A troublemaker.

07:05.591 --> 07:08.261
Or did they do anything
that would incur bad karma?

07:08.845 --> 07:10.471
Bad rumors?

07:10.555 --> 07:14.851
They were troublemakers, but no more
than your average junior high student.

07:15.726 --> 07:17.854
Wait. Bad karma…

07:18.396 --> 07:19.730
Could it be that?

07:20.314 --> 07:22.483
Bungee jumping from Yasohachi Bridge.

07:22.984 --> 07:24.694
A and B, you're still here?

07:24.777 --> 07:26.737
Yasohachi Bridge?

07:26.821 --> 07:28.489
A place known for suicides.

07:28.573 --> 07:31.200
It's a famous local hotspot
for paranormal activities.

07:31.284 --> 07:32.910
Right.

07:32.994 --> 07:37.081
It's popular among delinquents
to bungee jump from it.

07:37.165 --> 07:40.960
-It's the so-called bravery test.
-Which tribe do they belong to?

07:41.043 --> 07:43.463
There are many people dumber than me.

07:43.546 --> 07:45.131
How do they get the ropes?

07:45.214 --> 07:47.341
We won't do such a thing.

07:47.425 --> 07:51.304
I only heard it from people
of my parents' generation.

07:51.387 --> 07:52.346
One day,

07:53.139 --> 07:57.059
the four of them skipped school.

07:57.977 --> 08:00.730
It's nothing unusual,

08:00.813 --> 08:02.857
but after contacting their family,

08:02.940 --> 08:06.110
it turned out that
they didn't go home the night before.

08:06.861 --> 08:09.030
It was quite a fuss back then.

08:09.113 --> 08:13.409
Later, they were found lying
under the bridge.

08:13.493 --> 08:15.286
They were scolded badly,

08:15.369 --> 08:19.457
but they insisted that
they don't remember anything.

08:21.751 --> 08:23.753
I think we're in the right direction.

08:23.836 --> 08:26.672
I have been to Yasohachi Bridge.

08:26.756 --> 08:27.798
To do a bungee jump?

08:27.882 --> 08:29.217
Oh, god!

08:29.300 --> 08:32.136
Paranormal hotspots
accumulate curses easily,

08:32.220 --> 08:33.721
just like schools.

08:33.804 --> 08:37.391
So people from Jujutsu High
regularly patrol those places.

08:38.226 --> 08:40.269
There was nothing special back then.

08:40.353 --> 08:44.482
It was just a famous bridge
that everyone uses regularly.

08:44.565 --> 08:47.068
We should go and check it out.

08:47.652 --> 08:48.778
Yes.

08:48.861 --> 08:50.363
Fushiguro.

08:50.905 --> 08:53.824
Sorry, but I have something to ask you.

08:54.325 --> 08:55.326
What is it?

08:55.409 --> 08:59.121
She took care of me
when she was in school.

08:59.622 --> 09:02.250
How is Tsumiki doing?

09:03.668 --> 09:04.752
She's doing well.

09:04.835 --> 09:06.754
Who is Tsumiki?

09:07.505 --> 09:08.506
My sister.

09:08.589 --> 09:09.465
What?

09:09.549 --> 09:12.218
You never tell us anything about yourself!

09:12.301 --> 09:13.761
That's right!

09:15.137 --> 09:17.515
Why don't they…

09:18.474 --> 09:20.434
destroy these cursed relics?

09:20.518 --> 09:22.270
It's because they can't do it.

09:22.353 --> 09:24.230
Not with Special Grades, that is.

09:24.730 --> 09:28.526
They can only halt its life stream
and preserve its existence

09:28.609 --> 09:31.112
with a binding to stop it
from causing more damage.

09:31.195 --> 09:33.197
Sukuna's fingers are harmful too, right?

09:33.281 --> 09:34.949
That's an exception.

09:35.491 --> 09:39.662
After becoming a cursed object,
it is divided into 20 parts.

09:39.745 --> 09:43.040
It's a monster that can
still attract curses after all this time.

09:43.124 --> 09:46.043
That's why Sukuna chooses its vessel.

09:46.127 --> 09:47.712
I see.

09:47.795 --> 09:51.424
So I can choose anyone?

09:53.634 --> 09:55.553
Hey, you…

09:56.304 --> 09:58.431
Is it money you want?

09:58.514 --> 10:00.808
I don't have much money,

10:00.891 --> 10:02.935
but I can take a loan--

10:03.644 --> 10:05.938
It's okay.

10:06.022 --> 10:08.899
He still can't see me in this situation.

10:08.983 --> 10:10.568
He's really lacking talent.

10:10.651 --> 10:13.321
Here, open your mouth.

00:10:42.340 --> 00:10:43.424
We're here.

00:10:43.507 --> 00:10:46.594
Koinokuchi Canyon, Yasohachi Bridge.

00:10:46.677 --> 00:10:50.139
I'll cast the Veil immediately
once a Curse Spirit is confirmed.

00:10:51.098 --> 00:10:52.642
Got it!

00:10:54.477 --> 00:10:57.647
Hey, sorry to disturb you
although you just woke up.

00:10:58.481 --> 00:11:01.233
Can you run some errands for me?

00:11:11.285 --> 00:11:14.872
Come on, we can't even
find a trace of the curse.

00:11:15.873 --> 00:11:16.749
SPICY COD ROE

00:11:16.832 --> 00:11:20.127
I don't feel any residuals or aura.

00:11:20.711 --> 00:11:21.796
Really?

00:11:21.879 --> 00:11:23.381
Then we might have been wrong.

00:11:23.464 --> 00:11:24.799
Let's start over again.

00:11:24.882 --> 00:11:27.176
I think we better not waste too much time.

00:11:27.259 --> 00:11:28.469
Why not?

00:11:28.552 --> 00:11:31.806
That's a famous paranormal hotspot, right?

00:11:31.889 --> 00:11:34.683
Someone else could be cursed too.

00:11:35.267 --> 00:11:38.312
Furthermore, the death rate
is 100% as it stands.

00:11:38.896 --> 00:11:41.023
We can't afford to lose any more lives.

00:11:41.107 --> 00:11:42.817
That's right.

00:11:42.900 --> 00:11:44.068
Aha!

00:11:44.151 --> 00:11:46.320
Bungee jumping
used to be famous there, right?

00:11:46.404 --> 00:11:48.823
So wouldn't jumping down be the key?

00:11:48.906 --> 00:11:51.534
Did she just say, "Aha"?

00:11:51.617 --> 00:11:53.285
Yes, she did!

00:11:53.369 --> 00:11:55.830
Itadori has tried that.

00:11:55.913 --> 00:11:56.831
What?

00:11:59.041 --> 00:12:03.087
Wait! Did you jump
using that vinyl string?

00:12:05.548 --> 00:12:08.217
SCREAMING

00:12:08.300 --> 00:12:10.803
I found you! That's great!

00:12:11.387 --> 00:12:12.638
Fushiguro!

00:12:13.639 --> 00:12:14.807
Who's that again?

00:12:14.890 --> 00:12:16.684
Fushiguro's junior, right?

00:12:16.767 --> 00:12:19.019
-You kept teasing him earlier.
-Oh, right!

00:12:19.103 --> 00:12:21.689
You guys were talking about
Yasohachi Bridge.

00:12:21.772 --> 00:12:23.524
I'm glad I found you guys.

00:12:24.483 --> 00:12:25.526
Fujinuma?

00:12:26.777 --> 00:12:27.820
She's my ex-classmate.

00:12:28.320 --> 00:12:29.655
She's my sister.

00:12:30.865 --> 00:12:34.034
Great. You still remember me.

00:12:34.118 --> 00:12:38.539
I told her about Fushiguro yesterday.

00:12:38.622 --> 00:12:42.751
My neighbor, Morishita,
had a funeral at their house.

00:12:44.253 --> 00:12:49.550
My brother said that
you're investigating Yasohachi Bridge.

00:12:49.633 --> 00:12:53.053
I wonder if these
two things are connected?

00:12:55.931 --> 00:12:57.141
What do you mean?

00:12:57.224 --> 00:13:00.853
I mean Morishita's death and that bridge…

00:13:00.936 --> 00:13:03.814
-It's unrelated. We're just…
-I…

00:13:04.398 --> 00:13:05.858
I have been to that bridge.

00:13:05.941 --> 00:13:09.069
I went there at night
during my sophomore year.

00:13:09.904 --> 00:13:11.071
Oh, my…

00:13:11.155 --> 00:13:14.992
Did any strange things happen
in your house recently?

00:13:15.075 --> 00:13:18.787
For example, a strange feeling that
only you experience at home.

00:13:21.832 --> 00:13:25.794
My family runs a local specialty store.

00:13:26.545 --> 00:13:31.800
But when I go back alone,
the automatic doors are wide open.

00:13:33.052 --> 00:13:36.889
My parents said it was just a coincidence,

00:13:37.515 --> 00:13:40.601
but there's definitely something there.

00:13:41.477 --> 00:13:42.770
I'm scared.

00:13:43.771 --> 00:13:47.483
At this moment, I heard about
Fushiguro investigating this incident.

00:13:47.566 --> 00:13:50.319
I recalled the incident
at Yasohachi Bridge.

00:13:50.402 --> 00:13:53.447
When did the automatic door
incident start?

00:13:53.531 --> 00:13:57.201
Exactly a week ago.
It happens every other day.

00:13:57.701 --> 00:13:59.328
It took at least two weeks

00:13:59.411 --> 00:14:04.083
for the four victims to die
after the abnormalities started.

00:14:04.166 --> 00:14:06.085
There's still some time.

00:14:06.168 --> 00:14:09.880
You didn't go
to Yasohachi Bridge alone, right?

00:14:09.964 --> 00:14:11.840
Do you recall who else was there?

00:14:11.924 --> 00:14:16.470
-So those two incidents are related?
-They are related to automatic doors.

00:14:16.554 --> 00:14:19.932
But it has nothing to do
with Morishita's death.

00:14:20.015 --> 00:14:24.103
I'm writing a university report,
so I asked them to help me.

00:14:24.186 --> 00:14:26.272
It's titled,
"The Impact of Paranormal Hotspots

00:14:26.355 --> 00:14:28.607
on Electromagnetic Waves
and Electronic Products."

00:14:28.691 --> 00:14:30.442
It's lame, right?

00:14:30.526 --> 00:14:33.112
But I want to hear from
as many people as possible.

00:14:33.195 --> 00:14:35.781
I hope you can tell me who went with you.

00:14:36.490 --> 00:14:39.285
Since I lied, I must save her.

00:14:42.246 --> 00:14:45.541
I went there with two seniors in the club.

00:14:46.125 --> 00:14:47.835
By the way, Fushiguro,

00:14:47.918 --> 00:14:50.296
Tsumiki was there too at that time.

00:14:51.463 --> 00:14:54.300
-Tsumiki?
-Fushiguro's sister!

00:14:55.968 --> 00:14:59.555
Really? I'll go ask Tsumiki, then.

00:14:59.638 --> 00:15:03.475
Well then, I'll send them home first.

00:15:03.559 --> 00:15:06.145
Please take over from here.

00:15:06.228 --> 00:15:08.147
Is there something wrong?

00:15:08.230 --> 00:15:11.150
I can't let you two
go back with a bicycle.

00:15:19.366 --> 00:15:20.576
Fushiguro.

00:15:22.286 --> 00:15:23.329
Fushiguro!

00:15:25.623 --> 00:15:27.333
Fushiguro, snap out of it.

00:15:27.416 --> 00:15:29.293
Confirm her safety first.

00:15:33.297 --> 00:15:34.465
I'm fine.

00:15:34.548 --> 00:15:36.800
I'm sorry. Please excuse me.

00:15:44.683 --> 00:15:46.185
I understand the situation.

00:15:46.268 --> 00:15:48.270
You need protection for Tsumiki, right?

00:15:48.354 --> 00:15:53.025
However, only Grade 2
Jujutsu Sorcerers are available now.

00:15:53.108 --> 00:15:54.610
Grade 2?

00:15:54.693 --> 00:15:58.697
If the threat is greater than expected,

00:15:58.781 --> 00:16:01.617
then we need to reexamine
the level of the curse.

00:16:03.118 --> 00:16:08.248
You're probably assigned this task
due to Itadori's growth.

00:16:08.791 --> 00:16:11.460
If the threat continues to rise,

00:16:11.543 --> 00:16:14.004
even Grade 2 Jujutsu Sorcerers
will not suffice.

00:16:14.588 --> 00:16:16.507
It's equally dangerous for all of you.

00:16:16.590 --> 00:16:19.176
I would recommend that you retreat first.

00:16:21.095 --> 00:16:22.513
What should I do?

00:16:23.180 --> 00:16:25.224
Should I go back on my own first?

00:16:25.975 --> 00:16:29.186
No, this task is dangerous
even if the three of us work together.

00:16:29.687 --> 00:16:31.397
I can't leave it to the two of them.

00:16:32.106 --> 00:16:34.650
Mr. Gojo will return next week.

00:16:35.192 --> 00:16:36.902
Until then…

00:16:37.611 --> 00:16:40.447
No, I can't afford to wait anymore!

00:16:40.948 --> 00:16:43.117
If the Cursed Spirit
does not attack proactively

00:16:43.200 --> 00:16:46.996
and only activates its cursed technique
within its marks,

00:16:47.079 --> 00:16:49.373
then it's useless to stay by her side.

00:16:49.873 --> 00:16:51.750
I have to exorcise it now!

00:16:52.251 --> 00:16:54.837
Why were you talking to Mr. Ijichi?

00:16:54.920 --> 00:16:56.922
Is your sister all right?

00:16:57.715 --> 00:16:59.008
She's fine.

00:16:59.633 --> 00:17:02.136
The mission is getting more dangerous now.

00:17:02.219 --> 00:17:04.930
Other Jujutsu Sorcerers
will be taking over.

00:17:05.014 --> 00:17:06.932
You guys can go home.

00:17:09.018 --> 00:17:11.562
Wait. Why? We can go home first?

00:17:11.645 --> 00:17:13.022
What about you?

00:17:13.105 --> 00:17:15.691
I'll say goodbye to Mr. Takeda
before returning.

00:17:15.774 --> 00:17:16.775
Come on. Hurry up.

00:17:26.910 --> 00:17:29.371
Hello. Is this Ms. Nitta?

00:17:29.872 --> 00:17:31.415
I have something to ask you.

00:17:32.207 --> 00:17:33.834
It should be the sequence.

00:17:34.793 --> 00:17:38.589
Fujinuma didn't walk on the bridge.

00:17:39.089 --> 00:17:41.717
The bravery test was done
under the bridge.

00:17:42.760 --> 00:17:44.887
Itadori went under the bridge too.

00:17:44.970 --> 00:17:47.473
Jumping off the bridge
probably doesn't count.

00:17:47.556 --> 00:17:49.600
If the Cursed Spirit is within a barrier,

00:17:49.683 --> 00:17:51.351
then the sequence will be important.

00:17:51.435 --> 00:17:53.687
It needs to be at night, under the bridge,

00:17:53.771 --> 00:17:55.439
and one more condition…

00:17:56.190 --> 00:17:58.609
It's impossible to cast a domain

00:17:58.692 --> 00:18:01.612
using expanded
and sustained cursed technique.

00:18:02.112 --> 00:18:06.158
Which means, this domain
is similar to the unfinished one

00:18:06.241 --> 00:18:08.118
back at the detention center.

00:18:08.869 --> 00:18:11.038
But this time, it's helpful.

00:18:12.956 --> 00:18:14.958
I don't need a Veil.

00:18:18.545 --> 00:18:20.964
You never tell us anything about yourself.

00:18:21.048 --> 00:18:22.716
That's right.

00:18:24.301 --> 00:18:26.261
You're so out of your wits that

00:18:26.345 --> 00:18:28.013
you didn't notice us at all.

00:18:28.514 --> 00:18:31.225
You don't have to tell us
about everything,

00:18:31.308 --> 00:18:32.726
but at least rely on us.

00:18:33.560 --> 00:18:34.978
We're friends, right?

00:18:44.113 --> 00:18:45.364
Tsumiki…

00:18:47.825 --> 00:18:49.451
She is currently in a coma.

00:18:51.245 --> 00:18:56.625
The Yasohachi Bridge curse
will only appear in front of the cursed.

00:18:59.169 --> 00:19:01.505
Since she can't speak,

00:19:02.881 --> 00:19:05.092
there's no way to know
when she'll be killed.

00:19:07.845 --> 00:19:09.847
So I want to exorcise it right away.

00:19:10.973 --> 00:19:13.392
But it's true that the mission
is more dangerous now.

00:19:13.475 --> 00:19:16.019
All right, we got it.

00:19:16.103 --> 00:19:18.689
Just make it clear at the beginning.

00:19:24.361 --> 00:19:27.865
If the Cursed Spirit is within a barrier,
then the sequence will be important.

00:19:28.615 --> 00:19:30.701
It needs to be at night, under the bridge,

00:19:31.201 --> 00:19:32.619
and one more condition…

00:19:33.370 --> 00:19:37.332
There may be a river under the canyon.

00:19:42.754 --> 00:19:46.550
The act of crossing a river or a barrier…

00:19:47.509 --> 00:19:50.929
has significant meaning in sorcery.

00:20:03.400 --> 00:20:04.860
There it is.

00:20:07.029 --> 00:20:09.156
Seems like it will be worth exorcising.

00:20:23.420 --> 00:20:24.671
What is this?

00:20:25.339 --> 00:20:26.673
Someone's here first.

00:20:26.757 --> 00:20:27.674
What?

00:20:27.758 --> 00:20:30.177
Fushiguro, that's unrelated
to the curse, right?

00:20:30.260 --> 00:20:31.678
Yes.

00:20:32.846 --> 00:20:35.849
Then both of you focus on that one.

00:20:37.267 --> 00:20:39.228
Let me handle this one.

00:20:39.770 --> 00:20:44.149
What? Are you willing to play with me?

00:22:16.616 --> 00:22:18.535
-Juju Stroll.
-Juju Stroll.

00:22:19.286 --> 00:22:21.246
Someone, help! I got robbed!

00:22:26.835 --> 00:22:29.171
I run a Chinese restaurant.

00:22:29.254 --> 00:22:31.423
I'll treat everyone to a meal as thanks.

00:22:31.506 --> 00:22:32.716
You don't have to!

00:22:32.799 --> 00:22:36.178
Really? Thank you for your kindness!

00:22:37.179 --> 00:22:39.765
This restaurant has been passed down
for four generations.

00:22:39.848 --> 00:22:43.852
It was supposed to close
during my father's generation,

00:22:44.436 --> 00:22:47.981
but I insisted on
inheriting the restaurant.

00:22:48.982 --> 00:22:54.321
I want to pass on the restaurant
and the taste of our food.

00:22:54.404 --> 00:22:57.365
-Such a good story.
-Such a good story.

00:22:57.449 --> 00:22:59.284
Thank you for waiting.

00:22:59.367 --> 00:23:02.621
This is our signature dish,
fried dumplings set meal.

00:23:02.704 --> 00:23:04.331
-I'm digging in!
-I'm digging in!

00:23:05.248 --> 00:23:07.209
Thanks for the hospitality.

00:23:13.048 --> 00:23:14.216
Guys.

00:23:14.299 --> 00:23:18.386
What do you think about fried dumplings
with cabbage fillings?

00:23:18.470 --> 00:23:20.680
Well said, Fushiguro!

00:23:20.764 --> 00:23:24.351
Although she's a really nice person…

00:23:25.310 --> 00:23:29.481
But I think fried dumplings are considered
a vegetable dish, not a meat dish.

00:23:29.564 --> 00:23:30.565
Are you serious?
